      },
      {
        "step_number": 2,
        "title": "Steam the rice",
        "body": "Put the rice, 2 1/4 cups of the water, and the salt in a saucepan. Bring to a boil, cover, and simmer on low until tender, about 18 minutes. This runs under the stir-fry.",
        "ingredient_refs": [
          "long-grain-rice",
          "water",
          "kosher-salt"
        ]
      },
      {
        "step_number": 3,
        "title": "Stir-fry",
        "body": "Heat the neutral oil in a wok over high. Stir-fry the green beans in two batches until blistered and tender-crisp, about 4 minutes per batch. Set them aside. Stir-fry the shiitake about 2 minutes. Add the garlic and ginger for 30 seconds, then the chili bean sauce and the beans. Toss until the sauce clings. Off the heat, add the sesame oil and scallions. The stir-fry is about 12 minutes inside the 20-minute cook clock.",
